 "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=C.+Phil+Multifolds", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/seefeel/multifolds", "search": false}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/C.+Phil+Multifolds", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=C.+Phil+Multifolds", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/C.+Phil+Multifolds", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=C.+Phil+Multifolds&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“Underneath me at the moment is Multifolds by C. Phil.”", "the audio briefly looked like Steve Hughes - If You Were to Go, but the presenter said otherwise", "\"C. Phil\" is very likely a phonetic ASR mishearing of \"Seefeel\" (\"C\"+\"feel\"~\"Phil\"); Seefeel's real track \"Multifolds\" is from their 2024 Warp Records album \"Everything Squared.\""]}, {"t": 6872, "time": "01:54:32", "artist": "Bark Psychosis", "title": null, "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Bark+Psychosis", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Bark+Psychosis", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Bark+Psychosis", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Bark+Psychosis", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Bark+Psychosis", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Bark+Psychosis", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/artist/47870-Bark-Psychosis", "search": false}], "notes": ["“This is my last song before I sign it off to a lovely lunchtime show. This is one from Bach, Psychosis.”", "Bark Psychosis are a real English post-rock band (Hex, 1994; Codename: Dustsucker, 2004); \"Bach, Psychosis\" is an ASR mangling of the name, exact track not specified."]}], "counts": {"high": 10, "mid": 8, "low": 8}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:00:00", "end": "00:02:29", "text": "Streaming services are seeing this reflected in their catalogues. Deezer's study estimated that 50% of its daily music uploads and 34% of all of its music is AI generated. Apple Music cites a third of its monthly uploads. Though Bandcamp, Tidal and SoundCloud have put their foot down like the ARIA charts, enforcing a complete ban. There seems to be a few different regulatory approaches, but what do Aussie musicians think about all of this? Well, APRA AMCO surveyed Australian music creators and the results were pretty stark. 89% of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander musicians think that AI is going to worsen cultural appropriation, particularly by its use of their music to train models without their consent. Meanwhile, 82% of Aussie musicians are worried they might not be able to make a living from music anymore. And it's basically unanimous that something needs to change. 97% want policymakers to actually get across the issues around AI and copyright. Depressing stats aside, the music industry's activism has led to real change at the industry level, like what we've seen with the ARIA charts, but also at the government level. In July, the Prime Minister delivered a landmark address announcing a national framework and mandatory standards to regulate AI and protect local creative copyright. Ultimately, the message from artists, industry bodies like ARIA and the government is clear. AI can be a tool, but it shouldn't be a substitute for human creativity or a loophole to bypass consent and copyright. The ARIA ban is just the first line in a much bigger rulebook that's being written in real time. That was Maya talking about the news this week that the ARIA charts have banned AI music from being illegible. Backchat, your alternative to talkback on FBI 94.5. And that's all we've got time for today. Of course, a big thanks to our guests, Professor Catherine Lumley, Daryl Jones, Bex, and a big thanks to our producers, Elhesee Snellgrove, Tani Crookshank, Shia Highworth, Jasper Brady, and Maya Sathi. This has been Back Chat. We'll be back with the news from your city and beyond next week. But until then, stay tuned for Limsy Kimbo Up Now. Back Chat. Back Chat. Back Chat is produced by FBI Radio in Sydney. Tune in live every Saturday at 9.30am. Find more at fbi.radio or wherever you get your podcasts."}, {"start": "00:04:33", "end": "00:04:57", "text": "It's Lily here today. I also mix as Killian. I'm covering for Hugh. Before we go any further, I'd like to take a moment to acknowledge the traditional custodians of the land that we're broadcasting from today, the Gadigal people of the Eora Nation, and pay my respects to Elders past, present and emerging."}, {"start": "00:05:03", "end": "00:05:40", "text": "I haven't been in studio in a while so it's really nice to be back and also be at a time where people are awake. So if you want to text in you can on 0435 123 945. Love to hear from you. You can tell me what you're thinking about the music, what you had for breakfast. Yeah text in. Gonna keep it nice and soft for a bit. Got some nice ambient music and old slow kind of lo-fi post-rock to start and we'll see where we go thanks so much"}, {"start": "00:24:21", "end": "00:25:12", "text": "Hello, you're listening to Limbs Akimbo on FBi Radio with me, Killian. Had to throw a bit of hood in there. This one's my last August. Just to backtrack on some of the music we've listened to together, that last instrumental one was by Cancer House. It's called Camera Obscura. It's off Jessie Seppel's lovely label, Motion Ward. Above that, we had Sunstroke by Sepia Tone, how things were meant to be by quickly and at the top there that really lovely ambient song was called little heart by harold blood i'm gonna move into more electronic ambient territory for a little bit i hope you're enjoying and if you feel up to it you can text me on 0435 123 945 let's chat"}, {"start": "00:33:18", "end": "00:34:05", "text": "Hello, you tuned in to Limbs Akimbo on FBi Radio with me, Lily, or Killian covering for Hugh today. Underneath me at the moment we're listening to Foot Wrong by Moyne. Before that we had Spinning Out by Golden Star. So nice. And at the top there we had me referring to my track list. It's a track by Mallory. and i hope you're enjoying and it's so nice to hear what you're up to today got a message in from annika and amin who were on the way down to the south coast so nice i hope you guys enjoy your holiday yeah you can text in on 0435 123 945"}, {"start": "00:53:17", "end": "00:54:15", "text": "Hello, you're listening to Limbs Akimbo on FBi Radio with me, Lily. Just thought we'd go through some of the music we've been listening to together in this past little period of slower ambient music. Underneath me at the moment is Embody Source Energy by Florian T.M. Zek. Probably pronounced that wrong, I apologise, Florian. above that we had pieces by dj birdbath from theory therapy categorical label at the top there we had 114e hour by mark leclerc and we're also sending a big good luck to selena today for her exam from the salad family love that if you're enjoying it you can text in on 0435 123 945 It's nice to hear what you're up to today."}, {"start": "01:38:17", "end": "01:38:59", "text": "Hello, you're listening to Limbs Akimbo on FBi Radio with me, Lily, today covering for Hugh. Underneath me at the moment is Beyond Therapy by Synapsis, Synapses, Interrupt. Above that we had Niter by The Young Marble Giant, it's one of my favourites. And at the top there, that nice ambient one with a lovely piano through it is XB2 by Bot 1500. Thanks so much for sticking with me. it's my last half an hour so we're going to keep it a bit more upbeat you can text in on 0435 123 945 let me know how your day's going thanks so much"}, {"start": "01:46:54", "end": "01:47:46", "text": "Hello, you're listening to Limbs Akimbo on FBi Radio. Underneath me at the moment is Multifolds by C. Phil. Had to throw a bit in before the end of the show. And above that we had Round the Bend by Memotone. Played a few Memotone tracks today. Super nice. Also got a text in from Edward who's enjoying the music and is headed to Parramatta today to do a bit of history and sightseeing which i i love edward's asked if there's a good place to eat i'm not sure but if anyone else wants to shout out some spots in para you can text in on 0435 123 945 got 10 more minutes of me before we hand it over to lunchtime thanks for sticking with it"}, {"start": "01:57:55", "end": "01:58:23", "text": "Hello, you've been listening to Limbs Akimbo with Lily or Killian today. This is my last song before I sign it off to a lovely lunchtime show. This is one from Bach, Psychosis. Thanks so much for tuning in and for chatting today. It's been really nice to do this in the flesh. Thanks to Hugh and Jackson too. See you later."}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:02:00"}, "track": {"title": "Take Me to the Unknown (feat. Miette Hope)", "artists": [{"name": "Devin Hoffman"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:05:00"}, "track": {"title": "Little Heart", "artists": [{"name": "Harold Budd"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:07:07"}, "track": {"title": "How Things Were Meant To Be", "artists": [{"name": "Quickly"}, {"name": "Quickly"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:11:00"}, "track": {"title": "Teddy Bear Venom", "artists": [{"name": "Eternal Dust"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:15:00"}, "track": {"title": "Sunstroke", "artists": [{"name": "Sepiatone"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"e